// The service list a general contractor starts from — the benchmark's
// contractor book, all fourteen headings. Read ./index.js for the format and
// the rules. Almost none of these carried a pricing insight in the source, so
// most rows seed with no price and the screen says "set your rate". Where a
// row overlaps a trade FieldQuo already prices structurally (roofing, siding,
// gutters, insulation, cabinets), `existing` points there; the general
// contractor's own row still seeds, because a GC quotes the whole job.
